From: DeepAQ <5405949+DeepAQ@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: restore DS Params for 5 GHz START_AP

Port the 5 GHz AP compatibility fix from DeepAQ/openwrt-uwe5622-sunxi
commit 0539b491bc4552bd74e9d7bd79eb6df715b5b5b8 ("Fix 5GHz AP").

The vendor firmware START_AP path expects a DS Parameter Set IE while
hostapd normally omits that IE on 5 GHz. If DS Params are absent, recover
the primary channel from HT Operation and append a DS Params IE to the
driver's private beacon-head copy before the frame is handed to firmware.

Compared with the original DeepAQ change, harden the port for the current
standalone driver tree:
- bound the DS IE search to the actual IE bytes instead of passing the full
  head length from u.beacon.variable (which can read beyond the allocation);
- keep cfg80211_find_ie() results const;
- require a non-empty HT Operation body before reading the primary channel.

Only the private head buffer used to build WIFI_CMD_START_AP is modified.
The cfg80211/hostapd beacon template is left untouched.

Origin: https://github.com/DeepAQ/openwrt-uwe5622-sunxi/commit/0539b491bc4552bd74e9d7bd79eb6df715b5b5b8
Signed-off-by: Medvedolog <noreply@github.com>
---
 unisocwifi/cfg80211.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -1025,6 +1025,26 @@ static int sprdwl_cfg80211_start_ap(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 		head_len = beacon->head_len;
 		tail_len = beacon->tail_len;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Firmware START_AP compatibility: hostapd omits DS Parameter Set on
+	 * 5 GHz, while this firmware path expects a primary channel there.
+	 * Recover it from HT Operation and add DS Params only to our private
+	 * head copy. Do not modify cfg80211/hostapd's beacon template.
+	 */
+	if (head_len > offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u.beacon.variable) &&
+	    !cfg80211_find_ie(WLAN_EID_DS_PARAMS,
+			((struct ieee80211_mgmt *)head)->u.beacon.variable,
+			head_len - offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt,
+					    u.beacon.variable))) {
+		const u8 *ie = cfg80211_find_ie(WLAN_EID_HT_OPERATION,
+						 tail, tail_len);
+
+		if (ie && ie[1] >= 1) {
+			wl_ndev_log(L_ERR, ndev,
+				    "DS_PARAMS not present in beacon head, using channel %d from HT_OPERATION\n",
+				    ie[2]);
+			head[head_len++] = WLAN_EID_DS_PARAMS;
+			head[head_len++] = 1;
+			head[head_len++] = ie[2];
+		}
+	}
 
 	sprdwl_change_beacon(vif, beacon);
 
